[47.747, "o", "\r\n"]
[48.297, "o", "\u001b[38;5;253m●\u001b[0m Two different tmux servers — so my test was not landing where I am.\r\n"]
[49.197, "o", "  Let me identify my actual container:\r\n"]
[50.297, "o", "\r\n"]
[50.847, "o", "  \u001b[38;5;246mBash  cat /proc/self/cgroup && tmux -L console ls\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[51.547, "o", "\u001b[38;5;174m· Investigating…\u001b[0m \u001b[38;5;246m(31s · ↓ 0.8k tokens)\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[53.547, "o", "\r\n"]
[54.097, "o", "\u001b[38;5;253m●\u001b[0m Same container — the difference is the tmux socket. I'm on a named\r\n"]
[54.997, "o", "  socket `console`; the unit created its session on the default socket,\r\n"]
[55.897, "o", "  so it's invisible to your `tmux ls`.\r\n"]
[57.097, "o", "\u001b[38;5;253m●\u001b[0m Found it: the image's entrypoint creates that socket, running for the\r\n"]
[57.997, "o", "  container's full 10-day uptime. That's the server to join. Fixing the\r\n"]
[58.897, "o", "  unit and letting GitOps deploy it.\r\n"]
[60.197, "o", "\u001b[38;5;174m· Deploying…\u001b[0m \u001b[38;5;246m(2m 14s · ↓ 1.9k tokens)\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[62.197, "o", "\r\n"]
[62.747, "o", "\u001b[38;5;253m●\u001b[0m \u001b[38;5;114mWorking and verified end to end.\u001b[0m `tmux ls` now shows both:\r\n"]
[63.647, "o", "  claude:  1 windows (created Wed Aug 19 20:20:53 2026)\r\n"]
[64.247, "o", "  console: 4 windows (created Sun Aug  9 11:08:46 2026)\r\n"]
[65.247, "o", "\u001b[38;5;253m●\u001b[0m The unit created the session unprompted — which is the real proof,\r\n"]
[66.147, "o", "  since that's the same path a boot takes.\r\n"]
